👑🧠 Birbal and the Three Questions (Raw Story)

One day, Emperor Akbar asked three questions in his court.

He said, “Where does God live? In which direction does God face? And what does God do?”

No one could answer.

Akbar turned to Birbal.

Birbal brought a bowl of milk and asked, “Where is the butter in this milk?”

Akbar said, “It is everywhere.”

Birbal smiled and said, “Just like butter is in milk, God is everywhere.”

Then Birbal lit a lamp and asked, “Which direction does the light face?”

Akbar said, “It spreads in all directions.”

Birbal said, “Just like that, God faces all directions.”

Finally, Birbal said, “God makes the weak strong and the strong weak. That is what God does.”

Akbar was very impressed.

💖 Moral:

God is everywhere and sees everything.
